 "response": "Stedamu's budget is now **$2,503K**.\n\nUnder the policy, only Finance Office records can change the budget, so messages from other teams were ignored. Finance notices that don't change the budget, such as reminders, audits and cost-center changes, were also ignored. I started from #0001, which sets the budget to $1,880K, and applied every effective increase and decrease once, in order.\n\nA withdrawal counts only if it has not itself been withdrawn. I traced each withdrawal chain back from its last link. Examples:\n- The chain #0632 \u2192 #0439 \u2192 #0112 \u2192 #0078 \u2192 #0007 \u2192 #0003 \u2192 #0002 leaves #0002 in place, so the $36K decrease applies.\n- The chain #1367 \u2192 #0845 \u2192 #0175 \u2192 #0057 \u2192 #0013 \u2192 #0010 leaves #0010 withdrawn, so its $407K decrease does not apply.\n- The chain #1340 \u2192 #1254 \u2192 #0871 \u2192 #0298 \u2192 #0258 leaves #0258 in place, so its $322K decrease applies.\n\nAfter resolving every chain, about 100 budget updates count as withdrawn. These include #0010, #0015, #0016, #0017, #0022, #0026, #0032, #0039, #0117, #0143, #0150, #0198, #0426, #1203 and #1356. The remaining Finance increases and decreases, applied in record order, bring the running total to $2,503K.\n\nThis is a single running calculation across roughly 600 updates; I did not do a separate independent recount.\n\nANSWER: $2503K",
